{
 "what": "PR #416: structured design critique of beach crest V2 over the sunset middle-ground sea (window.__RAW_BEACH_WASH__='sunset'), and the refinement it produced (V2.1). Variants in the engine: v1 = beach as it draws (D-035), sf = sunset sea + first sunset crest (window.__RAW_BEACH_CREST_V2__='first'), sunset = sunset sea + V2.1.",
 "owner_request": "2026-10-21 ~02:00 EDT: 'I want you to use art skills, run a structured design critique with colour-harmony checks across all three crests, to make sure we're making this fit our middle ground best as possible'",
 "method": "crit.mjs (scratchpad; wave-lib model): worst case over world/regional/coastal alpha x swell lighting 0/0.5/1 x every 0.05 m, whitecap off/on: APCA |Lc| body and whitecap front, CIEDE2000, coloraide-port dichromats, self-contrast (z 3-4.9 band centre; below 1.05 m); hue relation ink vs local sea (OKLCH), blue-yellow separation, seam at the switch, energy cue 3 m vs 6 m, coastal repaint at the engine-measured crest cover, family distance to light V2 (D-036). Switch scan 1.9-2.8 m every 0.05. Engine: offline harness, paired exact wash (PAIRED=1), crest_contrast.py --theme beach, repaint_frames.py (mean OKLab of sea pixels with vs without crests).",
 "decision_inside_the_candidate": {
  "kept": "warm inks oxblood / pale lemon + lemon (owner direction)",
  "changed": [
   "switch 2.1 -> 2.4 m (on the sea anchor; best worst-case body |Lc| of the scan)",
   "storm peach -> blush [1.00,0.84,0.88] (repaint 48-59 -> 1-13 deg model; 19 -> 2 deg engine)",
   "foam follows the ink: oxblood-black [0.08,0,0] below the switch, white above (whitecap front |Lc| 24.9 -> 38.5)"
  ],
  "rejected": [
   "light family umber/cream/gold (gold storm repaints the purple sea 99-133 deg)",
   "aubergine dark ink (blue-yellow separation 0.005 -> 0.044 for dichromats on small seas, best self-contrast, but cool, not the warm direction)",
   "wine dark ink (no measurable gain)",
   "lilac storm (as good as blush, cooler)"
  ]
 },
